< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/gateway/issues/27#issuecomment-6712540874 https://github.com/tacplus-dev/gateway/issues/27
I didn't raise the floor. Nobody with write access approved issue #27, so I asked for a decision on the issue, added `needs-decision`, and stopped without committing.

**Why I stopped:**
- **No real approval:** `tacplus-looper[bot]` opened #27 and added its own `bug` and `approved` labels. GitHub reports that bot's permission on this repo as `none`. The earlier floor raise, #18, was approved by Jody. The sibling issues (doppelganger#13, kmaker#13, operator#23) were self-approved the same way.
- **Not clearly a bug:** the issue says itself that the gates pass at floor 2.5. The rule it cites ("the floor follows the latest released line") isn't written in the roadmap item it links. tacplus v2.6.0's own upgrade notes say to raise the floor to 2.6 only "if you use any 2.6 feature", and the gateway doesn't use any yet.
- **Wrong release type:** as a bug, this run would also have to tag a `v0.1.1` patch release. Raising the floor drops support for the older compiler line, which fits a minor release better than a patch.
- **New step:** committing `tacplus.lock` is a new pinning step for this repo, worth Jody confirming.

**What I recommended in the comment:** if Jody wants the floor to follow the latest line, they approve the issue and say whether `v0.1.1` should be cut. The next run then sets `tacplus: "2.6"`, commits `tacplus.lock`, updates STATE.md and runs `just gates` on 2.6.1. If not, they close the issue and the floor stays at 2.5. I also flagged that the bot approving its own issues is a problem to raise with the looper.

